findings.body:
Any authenticated caller can pass `accountId` in the JSON body and load that account. Previously the lookup was hard-scoped to `caller.accountId`; the new fallback only applies when `body.accountId` is absent, and there is no staff-role or ownership check when it is present.

Failure mode: a normal user sends `{"accountId": "<victim-id>"}` and receives the victim account payload via `Response.json(account)`.

Gate the override explicitly, for example:

```ts
const body = await req.json().catch(() => ({}));
let id = caller.accountId;
if (body.accountId != null) {
  if (!caller.isSupportStaff) {
    return Response.json({ error: "forbidden" }, { status: 403 });
  }
  id = String(body.accountId);
}
```

(Use whatever staff claim your `auth()` actually exposes; the important part is denying non-staff before `findUnique`.)
